WEBVTT

NOTE
What is on screen at each moment of the flythrough, for a reader who does not
know the site. The animation is silent, so nothing here is a transcript of
anything — the cues name the building being flown past.

Timings were read off the film at five-second intervals; the shot boundaries are
where the camera arrives somewhere, not hard cuts, because there are none. If
the flythrough is ever re-cut these all move. See assets/README.md.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.500
The whole site, from above Rice Road. Nothing here is built.

2
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:17.000
Coming up the drive from the car park.

3
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:26.000
Building A, the church. The steps climb sixteen feet from the car park to the doors.

4
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:33.000
At the top of the steps, beside the church.

5
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:45.000
The piazza — the paved court the three buildings enclose.

6
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:58.000
Building B's covered walk, along the north side of the court.

7
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:09.000
Back at the west front. The great arch is glazed above the doors.

8
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:22.000
Building C, the diocese centre, from the car park.

9
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:33.000
Building B: Sunday school below, senior housing above.

10
00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:50.000
Rising over the site. 190 parking spaces wrap the outside.

11
00:01:50.000 --> 00:02:20.000
The roofs: barrel vaults over the nave and the aisles, a dome over the crossing.

12
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:55.000
Around the east end, where the three altars stand.

13
00:02:55.000 --> 00:03:20.000
The west front, the steps and the piazza, from above.

14
00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:30.000
Five and a half acres at 169 Rice Road. Filed with the town; not yet approved.
